    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green (28/28, including the new `Cp17Tests`).\n\n## What I did\n\n`locality` is a read-only, purely-derived field (like `displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`), so no persistence was needed \u2014 it's computed at DTO-mapping time:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (documenting the fixed table: Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD; `UNKNOWN` otherwise). The generator produces `OwnerDto.locality`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = ...)` that maps the city through the table inline, returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n\n## One trap worth flagging\n\nMy first attempt put the lookup in a `default String deriveLocality(String city)` helper on the mapper interface. That compiled cleanly but **broke every owner-create**: MapStruct treats any `String\u2192String` method on a `@Mapper` as an implicit conversion and applied it to *all* String properties in the reverse `toOwner` mapping \u2014 so an incoming telephone `0400000004` was silently replaced with `\"UNKNOWN\"`, failing E.164 validation with a 400. It presented as an unrelated telephone bug across all 16 create-based checkpoints.\n\nThe fix was to write the derivation as a **pure inline expression** with no helper method on the interface (matching how `membershipTier` is done). I've saved this pitfall to memory since it's a non-obvious repo-wide hazard.",
